invariant: INV-26
file: ct.h
catches: test/quic-builds.sh
reason: a TRANSPORT=quic-nonblocking build takes the AES-GCM suites on the
  AES=soft table, so quic_packet.c hands the S-box the Handshake and 1-RTT
  packet and header protection keys, which come from traffic secrets, and
  the table is indexed with them. The TLS suite build still refuses the
  table, so only the QUIC check sees it: quic-builds.sh compiles
  quic_packet.c under the suite on AES=soft and requires the refusal.

--- old
#if !defined(CH_CPU_RUNTIME) && !defined(CH_AES_EXTERN)
--- new
#if !defined(CH_CPU_RUNTIME) && !defined(CH_AES_EXTERN) && !defined(CH_TRANSPORT_QUIC_NONBLOCKING)
